// Title: Potential Persistence Via Logon Scripts - Registry
// Sigma ID: 9ace0707-b560-49b8-b6ca-5148b42f39fb
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Tom Ueltschi (@c_APT_ure)
// Date: 2019-01-12 | Modified: 2025-10-26
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, T1037.001, persistence, lateral-movement
// Description: Detects creation of "UserInitMprLogonScript" registry value which can be used as a persistence
//   method by malicious actors
// False positives:
//   - Investigate the contents of the "UserInitMprLogonScript" value to determine of the added script is legitimate
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/f339e7da7d05f6057fdfcdd3742bfcf365fee2a9/atomics/T1037.001/T1037.001.md
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_persistence_logon_scripts_userinitmprlogonscript.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey contains "UserInitMprLogonScript"
